h protecting groups.\n\nTool: detect_functional_groups\nDescription: Detects functional groups in a molecule represented by a SMILES string.\nArguments:\n- smiles (str, required): SMILES string of the molecule to analyze.\n\nTool: detect_protection_groups\nDescription: Detects protecting groups in a molecule and their positions.\nArguments:\n- smiles (str, required): SMILES string of the molecule to analyze.\n\nTool: apply_template\nDescription: Applies a retrosynthetic template to a molecule. If one template is applicable to different groups, all possible outcomes are returned.\nArguments:\n- molecule_smiles (str, required): SMILES string of the target molecule.\n- template_id (str, required): Identifier of the retrosynthetic template to apply.\n\nTool: verify_step\nDescription: Verifies if a retrosynthetic step is valid. This tool might fail for intramolecular reactions.\nArguments:\n- molecule_smiles (str, required): SMILES string of the target molecule.\n- template_id (str, required): Retrosynthetic template in SMARTS format.\n- precursors (list[str], required): List of SMILES strings representing the precursor molecules.\n\nTool: verify_route\nDescription: Verifies if a synthesis route follows the expected schema.\nArguments:\n- route (str, required): JSON string representing the synthesis route.\n\nTool: search_catalog_by_smiles\nDescription: Searches a catalog for available precursors.\nArguments:\n- smiles_list (list[str], required): List of SMILES strings representing the chemicals to search for.\n- limit (int, optional, default: 5): Maximum number of results to return. Default is 5.\n\nTool: is_buyable\nDescription: Checks if a list of molecules are commercially available.\nArguments:\n- smiles_list (list[str], required): List of SMILES strings representing the molecules to check.\n\nTool: map_reaction_smiles\nDescription: Maps atoms in a reaction SMILES string using attention-guided atom mapping. Sometimes, the mapping may help to get the templates to wor